Unreleased

	[ Nils Schimmelmann ]
	* quantize: take the floor from the group total and keep it out of the loop
	  - Derive the floor from the group total BlocQuant already holds, so M/S
	  frames use the same L/R total as the masking target
	  - Pass the floors in rather than a flag tested inside the band loop, which
	  GCC unswitched into a second copy of the loop
	  - Leave the floor off when PNS is disabled
	* blockswitch: sum each 128-sample half once
	  Sub-block windows are 256 samples at a hop of 128, so each half serves two
	  windows, yet every window was summed from scratch. Sum the nine halves of a
	  frame once and add pairs. The two-half sum rounds differently from one
	  256-term sum, but over 147 corpus clips at HE -q 50, -q 30 and -b 16 no frame
	  changes window type and the decoded audio is identical, and LC audio is
	  identical to master.
	  Instruction counts vs master on the benchmark's synthetic signals (arm64): LC
	  2 to 4% fewer (silence x0.958, music x0.978), HE -q 50 x1.007, geometric mean
	  x0.989; a low-rate HE encode, which now runs this analysis too, costs 4% more
	  instead of 7%.
	* quantize: try each band one scalefactor step coarser
	  Keep the step when the masking-weighted error it adds costs less than
	  the bits it saves. Only below 56 kbps per channel, where rate is scarce,
	  and only for bands whose magnitudes fit the small tables.
	* Drop provenance and cross-library history from comments
	* Reorder faad_decoder members to minimize struct padding gaps
	* blockswitch: span the same time above 48 kHz
	  The transient detector's 256-sample window covers half the time at
	  96 kHz, so a bass note's phase swings the first-difference energy and
	  trips short blocks on stationary material. Widen the window with the
	  rate so it spans the same 5.3 ms. Output at 48 kHz and below is
	  unchanged.
	* faac.h: export only from the DLL build on Windows
	  FAACAPI expanded to dllexport for every program that included the header.
	  The shared library now defines FAAC_BUILDING; everyone else declares plain
	  functions, which links against both the DLL import library and the static
	  library without a define because the API exports no data.
	* faac: write MP4 through libfaam and read RF64 and bounded WAV input
	  Replace faac's built-in MP4 writer with a thin libfaam adapter, and read
	  WAV input incrementally so large files encode without being loaded.
	  Default .m4a output matches master byte for byte, apart from PNG cover
	  typing and creation times past 2040.
	  - Write MP4/M4A through libfaam, keeping tags, gapless info, the custom
	  tag namespace and cover art.
	  - Parse RIFF and RF64 headers incrementally; honour the declared data
	  length, read to EOF when it is unknown, and let --ignorelength override
	  it. Read float WAV in either byte order.
	  - Buffer WAV reads and convert native 16-bit frames in batches.
	  - Add --faststart to write moov before mdat (off by default).
	  - Document the supported input and output formats and BMP covers.
	* libfaam: add the MP4 muxer/demuxer library and the faam tool
	  libfaam is a dependency-free ISO BMFF (MP4/M4A/M4B) muxer and demuxer
	  that works through caller-supplied I/O callbacks, so it suits camera,
	  SD-card and embedded recorders as well as files. faam is its command-line
	  tool. No encoder code changes.
	  Library:
	  - Mux and demux AAC, H.264 and H.265 tracks with tags, cover art,
	  chapters and gapless info; fragmented MP4 for crash-safe recording;
	  edit tags and chapters of a finished file in place.
	  - Write moov before mdat on request (FAAM_MUXER_FASTSTART) and report
	  mp4v video as a generic entry with its size and VOL header.
	  - Keep public structs append-only with flags in named enums, refuse I/O
	  requests above INT32_MAX, and allocate only through open and close.
	  Build:
	  - Add the encoder, muxer, muxer-video and muxer-fragmented options;
	  -Dencoder=false builds libfaam alone.
	  - Version the project 3.0.0 and the shared libraries SONAME 3.
	  - Export symbols only from the DLL build on Windows and check that the
	  tools do not import the FAAC DLLs.
	  Frontend:
	  - Share file helpers, creation-time handling and cover detection between
	  faac and faam; accept BMP artwork and reject creation times that do
	  not fit the MP4 fields. Move the endian helpers to common/.
	* quantize: raise the energy floors, lower the average-energy weight
	  AVG_ENERGY_WEIGHT 0.20 -> 0.10, AVG_ENERGY_FLOOR_FRAC 0.0010 -> 0.0020
	  (-27 dB), PEAK_ENERGY_FLOOR_FRAC 0.0050 -> 0.0200 (-17 dB).
	  LOUDNESS_EXPONENT stays at 0.40: 0.35 gained more MOS on the gate clips
	  but smeared HE attacks (haze gate atk_he_q50 +3.1 dB mean, +6.2 dB worst
	  kick).
	  Chosen from 63 grid points around master, scored on 126 held-out ABR
	  encodes (gate clips excluded), paired against master:
	  all  +0.0074 MOS  95% CI low +0.0014
	  HE   +0.0081 MOS
	  5 clips below -0.05, worst -0.081. Haze gate vs master constants: attack
	  smear +0.21 dB mean, +0.32 dB worst kick.
	  A higher PEAK floor (0.0400) scored +0.0127 but put five CBR clips past
	  -0.10 in CI (worst -0.35, 12-German-male-speech at 48k_stereo_16k) at
	  unchanged bitrate. This point keeps those five above -0.10 locally, but
	  they were picked because they failed, so that is a weak check.
	* sbr: code time deltas and couple stereo envelopes when cheaper
	  Per envelope, pick the cheaper of frequency-delta and time-delta coding,
	  and for stereo pairs the cheaper of L/R and level/balance coupling. The
	  previous frame's last envelope is kept per channel by access-unit parity,
	  so a frame the rate loop writes twice codes against the same reference.
	  Time-delta books carry only the central entries (|d| <= 6); a wider jump
	  is always cheaper as frequency deltas.
	  Envelope levels are now clamped to the codable delta range as they are
	  quantized, so the frequency-delta chain never needs an escape.
	  The dry-run write no longer advances the reference, and the bitstream
	  writer indexes the channel pair correctly.
	  Saves about 33 bits/frame/channel of SBR payload on non-FIXFIX frames,
	  which rate control hands to the core: +0.03 to +0.06 MOS at 24-48 kbps
	  stereo, ~0 at 64 kbps.
	* sbr: code time deltas, couple envelopes, and vectorize QMF analysis (#7)
	  Choose frequency or time deltas for SBR envelopes and noise floors, and
	  couple a stereo pair when that codes smaller. Store absolute envelope
	  levels with the same frequency-delta limits and retain frame references
	  across rate-control retries. Saved SBR bits go to the AAC core.
	  Sum Huffman lengths when choosing deltas and pack the normative books
	  into 16-bit entries. Size candidate payloads through the shared writer.
	  Mirror the exact QMF filter taps and separate contiguous polyphase
	  filtering from rotation so GCC can vectorize both loops. Reuse the FFT
	  output buffer as workspace. Reserve the ADTS header and write it once
	  the payload size is known. Correct the ASC sync-extension comment.
	  GCC 13.3, -O3 and LTO: text + rodata + data falls from 77936 to 76136
	  bytes, 88 bytes below upstream/master. Updated benchmark suite HE
	  instruction counts fall 14.57% versus the first footprint pass; paired
	  180-second workloads use about 17% less HE CPU time. LC instruction
	  counts are essentially unchanged.
	  Raw AAC and ADTS match the pre-optimization branch across 384 cases
	  covering LC/HE, ABR/VBR/CBR, caps, rates and channel counts. ASC bytes
	  match upstream in 56 supported configurations; MPEG-2 still rejects
	  ASC. All QMF taps and Huffman codes retain their original bits.
	* quantize: silence dither-level frames
	  LSB dither sits above the 0.4 RMS silence gate and was coded at full
	  relative SNR: 400+ kbps for flat dither at -q 700. Frames whose mean
	  level over the energy-bearing bands is under 40 RMS are now silent.
	  Flat dither drops to ~8 kbps; the 118-clip VBR gate is MOS-neutral.
	* sbr: add a 4-envelope tier for steady frames
	  Steady frames split into 2 envelopes from 17 kbps per channel. With time
	  deltas coding the extra envelopes cheaply, try 4 from 36 kbps per channel
	  (placeholder, to be swept).
	  - raise SBR_MAX_ENVELOPES to 4; VARFIX still carries two
	  - FIXFIX writes log2 of the envelope count
	  - VARFIX bs_pointer is a fixed 2 bits, replacing an assert that no
	  longer constrained anything
	  LC and HE below the threshold are byte-identical to master. Library
	  .text grows 256 bytes.
	* sbr: add 4-envelope tier for FIXFIX SBR frames
	  Extend non-transient (FIXFIX) SBR frames to support 4 envelopes when operating
	  at or above SBR_FOUR_ENV_BITRATE_BPS (36000 bps/ch).
	  - Raise SBR_MAX_ENVELOPES to 4 in sbr.h and sbr_analysis.h
	  - Define SBR_FOUR_ENV_BITRATE_BPS as 36000u
	  - Emit log2(num_env) in FIXFIX grid writer (2 bits: 0 for 1, 1 for 2, 2 for 4)
	  - Keep VARFIX frames fixed at 2 envelopes and update VARFIX bs_pointer assert
	  - Audit all envelope loops, arrays, delta choices, and reference storage
	* sbr: build spec-compliant two-region master table
	  Past a k2/kx ratio of 2.2449 the spec splits the master table at 2*kx and
	  lets bs_alter_scale widen the upper region's bands. FAAC only ever built one
	  region, which was safe at bs_start_freq 15 but gives a table that disagrees
	  with the decoder's at any lower crossover: every envelope then lands in the
	  wrong band. Follow the spec algorithm, including the re-sort after the
	  upper region's narrowest band is widened.
	  Output is unchanged at the current crossover.
	* quantize: floor the VBR step at two LSB for all input
	  Constant relative quality coded dither, fade tails and near-silence at
	  the rate of loud music. At normal listening level the reference encoder
	  does not, so floor the step at an absolute level: quiet 24-bit and 16-bit
	  music now matches its rate at equal MOS. VBR only.
	* Add DAB+ 960-sample core and ADIF support with decoder-dab option
	* faac: update SBR resampling filter
	* Use PNS level 6 at or above 192 kbps
	* quantize: document masking parameters and units
	* quantize: use a compact stereo masking model
	  Keep masking parameters together and interpolate tilt gains directly per band. Remove the per-band tilt arrays and their configuration loops while retaining the fitted anchor points and stereo LC eligibility.
	* sbr: count payload bits without a scratch buffer
	  Allow bounded count-only PutBit streams and use them to size SBR payloads. Keep sizing and emission on the same writer path, remove the 2 KiB scratch array, and exercise count/write boundaries through Meson tests in CI.
	* quantize: retune the masking target for stereo LC at a set rate
	  For ABR/CBR plain stereo LC from 32 kbps per channel, take the loudness
	  exponent 0.35 and average-energy weight 0.15, steepen the treble
	  de-emphasis by 1.5x and apply a small frequency tilt (finer 1.5-3 kHz,
	  coarser around 11 kHz, finer above 18 kHz). VBR, HE-AAC, mono and
	  multichannel keep the original formula and stay bit-identical.
	  Parameters came from a coordinate search on 25 of the 49 benchmark clips
	  against Zimtohrli; the other 24 clips and 44.1 kHz were held out.
	* sbr: add two-region tables and count-only payload sizing
	* quantize: run scalefactor nudge with compact stereo masking model
	* Fix unused parameter in sbr.c, shadowed var in mux.c, and promote both to errors
	  Remove unused parameter 'sbr' from 'sbr_adopt_envelope_grid' in libfaac/sbr.c.
	  Fix variable shadowing of 'st' in 'faam_muxer_open' in libfaam/mux.c.
	  Configure meson.build to treat unused parameters and shadowed variables as errors (-Werror=unused-parameter and -Werror=shadow for GCC/Clang, /we4100 and /we4456-/we4459 for MSVC).
	* quantize: document tuned profile design and scalefactor nudging generalization
	* tns: implement complete ISO/IEC 14496-3 TNS engine
	* Include short-window TNS evaluation evidence
	* quantize: boost onset targets less below 2 kHz (LF exponent 0.25)
	  The onset gain lowered scalefactors by the same amount in every band, while
	  the scored pre-echo region is above 2 kHz. Take the square root of the gain below 2 kHz.
	* quantize: leave bands below 2 kHz unboosted at onsets
	  The onset gain lowered scalefactors by the same amount in every band, while
	  the scored pre-echo region is above 2 kHz. Skip the gain below 2 kHz.
	* filtbank: apply the onset boost only with the tuned masking profile
	  The boost was measured on stereo LC at 32 kbps per channel and up. Outside
	  that domain (mono, low rates, VBR, 5.1) CI shows lower MOS on 16 kHz speech
	  and 5-8% slower encodes at low rates, so leave those targets alone.
	* tns: filter short windows whose onset starts late
	  Port the short-window TNS filter (order 2, from 2.75 kHz) and apply it only to
	  windows the onset boost marks as late attacks: the first block holding a tenth
	  of the peak block's energy is block 4 or later. Long-window TNS and HE-AAC are
	  unchanged.
	  On the 77-clip 128 kbps set: pre-echo (NPER) over the 36 event clips falls
	  0.27 dB for dMOS -0.001; post-onset residual +0.04 dB. Dense-transient music
	  (fatboy) pays most of it. Text grows by about 4 KB.
	* frame: choose LC where the HE-AAC auto ceiling is reached
	  At one bit/s per channel per Hz LC gives up about 0.02 MOS for about 6 dB less pre-echo, inside HE-AAC's rate lead. Below that rate LC costs 0.07 to 0.10 MOS, so HE-AAC stays.
	* filtbank: boost short-window targets at onsets in HE-AAC too
	  On the HE-AAC core the boost brings 2 to 8 kHz pre-echo to about FDK-AAC's level; the remaining gap is in the SBR region.
	* stats: count short-window TNS
	  The banner reported only long-block TNS, so short-window TNS could not be
	  told apart from not running. Count late-attack candidate windows, filtered
	  windows and short channels with TNS. Only built with -Dstats.
	* libfaad: name M/S mask modes with an enum
	* tns: use one filter direction for long and short windows
	  Both window types filter backward, so the direction field and the forward
	  recurrence go away. The direction bit is still written whenever a filter is
	  present.
	* tns: filter long windows backward
	  Run the long-window TNS filter from the high end of the spectrum and signal
	  direction 1. The LPC fit is unchanged; only which way the filter is applied to
	  the spectrum differs, so side info and bitrate stay the same.
	* libfaad: add the FAAD decoder and the faad tool
	* filtbank: boost short-window targets at onsets to cut pre-echo
	  Quantization noise in a short window spreads over the whole window, so
	  the quiet samples ahead of an attack carry it as pre-echo. Windows that
	  start quietly and then rise are coded finer.
	  - Measure each short window's first-difference energy in its first
	  quarter against its average, so the measure follows the high
	  frequencies where pre-echo is audible
	  - Turn the ratio into a per-window gain of at most ~10 and store it in
	  CoderInfo
	  - Share the 32-sample block energies between the overlapping windows
	  - Scale the band targets by the strongest gain in each short-window group
	  - Apply it to LC and to the HE-AAC core alike
	  - Leave long blocks and steady windows unchanged (gain 1)
	* Fix issue template redirect

2.2 (Sep 29, 2026)

	[ Robert Kausch ]
	* build: honor an explicit b_lto=false; drop __stdcall on x86 Windows

	[ Nils Schimmelmann ]
	* Bump the ABI to 2: faac_params_init() takes the caller's struct size
	* HE-AAC auto range 8-32 kbps per channel at 44.1 and 48 kHz (was
	  12-28), narrowing to 8-12 at 32 kHz; VBR up to -q 75 (was 60);
	  HE-AAC v1 for multichannel layouts up to 8 channels, with one SBR
	  fill element per SCE/CPE instead of one per frame
	* Rate control: signed bit account for ABR; a real bit reservoir for CBR
	  behind `--cbr`
	* Refit the ABR bandwidth curve from a sweep: a wider core at 24-56 kbps
	  stereo and every cutoff on the band grid reachable, where a double
	  snap had left seven
	* VBR codes at the top of the bandwidth curve (18750 Hz) instead of the
	  full band; `-q` and `-b` are exclusive; `-q` documented as a constant
	  quantizer quality, 1..5000, without bitrate anchors that drift
	* SBR: reconstruction toward 20 kHz; noise floor -18 dB; log-spaced band
	  table by rate; bs_stop_freq signals a k2 decoders actually accept;
	  envelopes measured over the slots the decoder applies them to, coded
	  in 3 dB steps, with two per frame without a transient from 17 kbps
	  per channel
	* Stereo: joint-stereo policy by rate; intensity on long windows below
	  40 kbps per channel, L/R on short windows below the crossover from 80;
	  short-window grouping and masking targets reworked; the sparsity mute
	  that zeroed a quiet unjoined channel's bands is gone; M/S codes the
	  side channel instead of dropping it and quantizes both halves against
	  the L/R level; long windows take it on every band from 32 kbps per
	  channel (24 on HE-AAC), short windows and HE-AAC at 20-24 kbps per
	  channel only below 1-2 kHz
	* A right-channel intensity band over a left PNS band is coded as PNS,
	  so decoders that apply intensity first don't play it silent
	* TNS on by default; frames screened before LPC analysis
	* Block switching: the HE core runs its own transient detector instead
	  of following SBR's, and both cores judge a sub-block's attack against
	  a running level instead of only its neighbour, so dense stationary
	  material stops defaulting to short windows
	* Quantizer: short blocks take the same loudness target as long ones
	  instead of 0.45x coarser, so transient frames stop losing bands to
	  PNS; from 56 kbps per channel the treble de-emphasis is steeper, so
	  the low bands get the margin; bands far below the frame's energy
	  are allowed coarser targets; kernels take band widths in quads and
	  vectorize fully, and grouping band energy is summed in four lanes
	* HUFF2: choose section codebooks jointly across each window group,
	  accounting for both codeword and section-header costs
	* Enforce the ISO/IEC 14496-3 per-channel frame ceiling and bitrate
	  limits; map channel counts to the standard AudioSpecificConfig/ADTS
	  channel configurations and reject non-standard counts
	* PNS and the MPEG version are now resolved by the encoder instead of
	  the caller: `faac_params` drops `pns_level` for a `use_pns` flag,
	  `faac_encoder_info` reports the resolved `mpeg_version`, and an
	  explicit MPEG-2 request silently upgrades to MPEG-4 for HE-AAC;
	  `faac` takes `--no-pns` in place of `--pns <0..10>`
	* frontend: MP4 output by default with detection from the extension;
	  24-bit packed PCM input; 64-bit mdat and duration; track language;
	  UTF-8 and wide-character paths on CLI and Win32 GUI; iTunes gapless
	  metadata (iTunSMPB); shared encoding engine and MP4 output in the GUI;
	  GUI opens on ABR at 128 kbps; optional end-of-encode diagnostics;
	  a PCM WAV could be read as float from an uninitialised header field;
	  endian conversion utilities unified, fixing a WORDS_BIGENDIAN check
	  that only worked because the macro happened to be undefined rather
	  than 0; help text and the man page corrected throughout
	* mp4write: container timing, HE-AAC sample rate declaration and gapless
	  fixes; GUI PCM clipping fix
	* HE-AAC: pad the pipeline delay to an even multiple of the core frame,
	  so gapless-aware decoders trim the right sample count at both ends
	* SBR: parameter resolution in VBR, tail drained on flush, psPresentFlag
	  for mono, less per-frame work in the writer
	* Pipeline draining during flush on short streams
	* Fix a 64 kHz short-window scalefactor band width table that summed
	  to 124 spectral lines instead of 128
	* Build the lookup tables and FFT twiddle factors shared between
	  encoder handles once per process instead of per open, so independent
	  handles can be opened concurrently without racing each other's tables
	* fft: replace the bit-reversed DIF kernel and its reorder pass with a
	  self-sorting Stockham kernel that lands in natural order directly
	* filtbank/channels: inline the window dispatch and simplify grouping
	  bit accounting for vectorization
	* Drop the never-selected KBD window from the filter bank
	* Drop dead count mode from bitstream writer
	* build: force-include config.h instead of per-file guards; drop the
	  cold/noinline hints on the HE-AAC frame path so PGO and -Os/-O3
	  make the call instead of a fixed attribute
	* frontend: show the git commit hash in `-h`, the GUI, verbose logging,
	  and the MP4 tag; `-h` reports the runtime libfaac version, not the
	  compile-time one

